#### Article 14

Powers of the Competent Authority in the field of prevention of domestic violence and protection of victims of domestic violence
1. In the field of prevention of domestic violence and protection of victims of domestic violence, the Competent Authority shall:
1) Develop the national strategy and coordinate the implementation of activities arising from it;

2) Ensure centralized registration of domestic violence cases in accordance with the procedure established by Government decree and include information from the Police, Investigative Committee, Special Investigation Service, the Prosecutor's Office and the Judicial Department of the Republic of Armenia, as well as data not registered by them and provided by support centers, guardianship and trusteeship bodies, and the National Competent Executive Authorities for education and healthcare; compile and annually publish relevant statistics on cases on its official website;
3) Study the root causes, conditions and consequences of domestic violence, develop programs to eliminate them;
4) Monitor compliance by shelters and their staff with the requirements established for them by the Government; license the provision of social services to victims of domestic violence through shelters by non-profit legal entities in accordance with the procedure established by the Government of the Republic of Armenia;
5) Establish shelters, conclude shelter financing agreements with non-profit legal entities according to the standard form approved by the Government, monitor the operation of shelters partially or fully financed by the Competent Authority, including control over the use of funds;
6) Organize regular training for staff of support centers and shelters and cooperate in this field with relevant non-governmental organizations;
7) Regularly publish a publicly available list of communication channels (including the telephone numbers of a free "Hotline" service for victims of domestic violence that support centers must have) that victims of domestic violence, members of their family and other persons can use to immediately contact an employee of the support center or a relevant specialist engaged by the center to receive free necessary assistance (in the case of persons with disabilities, this assistance shall also be accessible to them);
8) In accordance with the procedure established by the Government, open and manage an account for the provision of temporary assistance to victims of domestic violence. The account is replenished by allocations from the Government budget, donations from natural persons and legal entities and other lawful sources;
9) Approve the procedure for organizing and conducting the reconciliation process between the victim and the perpetrator of domestic violence;
10) Establish the monitoring procedure for prevention of domestic violence by adults subject to preventive registration;

11) Approve the rehabilitation program for perpetrators of domestic violence.
2. A Domestic Violence Prevention Council operates under the Head of the Competent Authority and provides recommendations to the latter on the national strategy for prevention of domestic violence, programs arising from the strategy, legislative reforms, public awareness activities and other issues. The Council members work on a pro bono basis. The Council has an equal number of:
